<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission acts to stop potato rot.</title>
<headline>EU Commission acts to stop potato rot.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commisson said on Wednesday it is putting forward a control directive to combat brown rot in potatoes.</p>
<p>The proposal, which follows concern about outbreaks of brown rot disease mainly in northern member states, will be put to EU farm ministers.</p>
<p>The European Union had been thought clear of the disease following the last outbreaks in the 1960s.</p>
<p>But, the Commission said in a statement, isolated outbreaks were recorded in the United Kingdom, Belgium and the Netherlands in 1995.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 Chris White</p>
</text>
